# Trivy ignore file for accepted vulnerabilities
#
# POLICY (2026-09-29, integration-keeper t_3b161655): an entry here is only
# acceptable if the corresponding finding is genuinely unresolved. An entry that
# suppresses a finding the image does not carry is dead weight at best and a
# concealed defect at worst -- it hides the day the finding becomes real. The
# wheel 0.42.0 entry (CVE-2026-24049) was exactly that: the final stage's purge
# ran before the site-packages overlay, so the base image's wheel 0.42.0
# survived into the shipped image and the suppression masked a live, fixable
# HIGH. The purge ordering is fixed in _build/Dockerfile.veid-pipeline and the
# entry is removed, so the gate must justify itself on the real image.
#
# The entries below are retained as accepted time-boxed risk. Documented in
# .vulnerability-allowlist.yaml and SUPPLY_CHAIN_SECURITY.md.
#
# NOTE: the "fixed in" annotations below are stale as of 2026-09-29 (the stack
# moved to tensorflow-cpu 2.20.0 / keras 3.15.0 / Pillow 12.3.0 / protobuf
# 5.29.6 / setuptools 83.0.0). They are left in place because the pinned
# versions no longer carry these CVEs; the entries are inert.


